WEBVTT

00:00:32.921 --> 00:00:36.591
HERMIONE: Why didn't it work for him,
the Elder Wand?

00:00:37.592 --> 00:00:39.511
It answered to somebody else.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.389
When he killed Snape,
he thought the wand would become his.

00:00:43.431 --> 00:00:47.727
But the thing is,
the wand never belonged to Snape.

00:00:47.769 --> 00:00:52.398
It was Draco who disarmed Dumbledore
that night in the astronomy tower.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.444
From that moment on,
the wand answered to him.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.280
Until...

00:00:59.322 --> 00:01:04.035
...the other night
when I disarmed Draco at Malfoy Manor.

00:01:04.077 --> 00:01:06.204
So that means....

00:01:07.747 --> 00:01:09.499
It's mine.

00:01:11.459 --> 00:01:12.877
RON:
What should we do with it?

00:01:14.003 --> 00:01:15.129
We?

00:01:15.505 --> 00:01:19.884
I'm just saying, that's the Elder Wand,
the most powerful wand in the world.

00:01:19.926 --> 00:01:23.847
With that, we'd be invincible.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.658
Together.

00:04:04.424 --> 00:04:05.925
[WOMEN LAUGH]

00:04:05.967 --> 00:04:08.136
FATHER:
Look after each other.

00:04:27.321 --> 00:04:29.240
-Bag?
-Yeah.

00:04:29.282 --> 00:04:30.324
Jumper?

00:04:31.993 --> 00:04:33.995
I'll miss you.

00:04:35.121 --> 00:04:36.831
RON:
Here they come.

00:04:52.013 --> 00:04:56.225
Dad, what if I am put in Slytherin?

00:04:58.519 --> 00:05:01.064
Albus Severus Potter...

00:05:02.356 --> 00:05:06.194
...you were named after two headmasters
of Hogwarts.

00:05:06.235 --> 00:05:07.987
One of them was a Slytherin...

00:05:08.029 --> 00:05:11.240
...and he was the bravest man
I've ever known.

00:05:13.117 --> 00:05:14.494
But just say that I am.

00:05:14.535 --> 00:05:20.291
Then Slytherin House will have gained
a wonderful young wizard.

00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:26.172
But, listen, if it really means that much
to you, you can choose Gryffindor.

00:05:26.214 --> 00:05:29.133
The Sorting Hat
takes your choice into account.

00:05:29.717 --> 00:05:31.886
-Really?
-Really.

00:05:31.928 --> 00:05:33.096
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

00:05:33.137 --> 00:05:35.932
GIRL: Bye, Mum.
CONDUCTOR: All aboard.

00:05:35.973 --> 00:05:37.141
Ready?

00:05:37.183 --> 00:05:38.726
Ready.

00:05:50.988 --> 00:05:52.740
BOY:
Come on, Jay, get a move on.

00:05:52.782 --> 00:05:54.367
JAMES:
Come on.

00:05:54.408 --> 00:05:55.952
[FROG CROAKING]

00:06:04.377 --> 00:06:07.213
[PEOPLE CHATTERING]

